From 3ee8aad499c586933f7c620fe6702af0049da68e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: miromraz <mraz.miro@seznam.cz>
Date: Sun, 31 May 2026 00:32:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] hexagonrpcd: ADSP sensor-registry support for Pixel 4a
 (sunfish)

The sunfish (sm7150) SLPI firmware crash-loops (sar.cc:27 chre_utils
fatal -> full ADSP SSR every ~10s) because mainline can't serve its
sensor registry the way the firmware expects. Each SSR tears down the
LPASS audio core, which is why speaker audio never gets a stable bit
clock. This adds the pieces needed for the firmware to build its
registry over FastRPC.

Write support (registry rebuild):
- apps_std: fopen 'w'/'a' modes + fwrite (method 5), backed by a
  writable leaf-open flag and a mapped write op.
- apps_std: mkdir (method 24) so the firmware can create its registry
  working dirs. ABI determined from the wire (in_nums=0, in_bufs=1);
  plumbed hexagonfs_mkdir -> mapped_mkdir (mkdirat, EEXIST ok).
- rpcd_builder: map sns_reg_version + temp.json siblings of the
  registry dir.

Listener robustness:
- Make unsupported handle/method/buffer-count non-fatal: report the
  error to the DSP and keep serving instead of exiting the listener
  (a single unsupported call used to kill the daemon and drop the
  registry service, restarting the crash loop).
- Raise the input-buffer cap 256B -> 64KB; the firmware writes its
  rebuilt registry (temp.json, ~2.7KB) in large chunks.

sns_registry reverse interface (WIP):
- Register an apps-side "sns_registry" local interface so the
  firmware's apps_remotectl_open() succeeds. Method 0 decoded as
  "read registry group by name" (e.g. "hw_platform"); response-data
  synthesis and the remaining methods are still to do.

cross-arm64.txt: meson cross file for building on a glibc x86_64 host
for a Debian aarch64 target.

With these, the firmware now fully reads its registry blobs/configs
and writes temp.json; remaining work is the sns_registry response
format (see project notes).
